# React Components

- Use functional components only; no class components
- One component per file; export a named function matching the file name
- Split when a file exceeds ~100 lines or mixes layout, data, and UI concerns
- Put reusable logic in custom hooks (`useX`), not inside large components
- Type props explicitly; never use `any`
- Colocate component CSS next to the component (`Component.tsx` + `Component.css`)
- Keep `App.tsx` as composition only: layout + sections, no business logic

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — multiple concerns in one file
export function Projects() {
  const [items, setItems] = useState([])
  useEffect(() => { fetch('/api').then(...) }, [])
  return <section>{/* 80 lines of markup */}</section>
}

// ✅ GOOD — hook + small presentational pieces
export function Projects() {
  const { items } = useProjects()
  return (
    <section>
      {items.map((item) => <ProjectCard key={item.id} project={item} />)}
    </section>
  )
}
```
